window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>\"If you're broken, I'll fix you . . . \"I'm only twenty-one and already damaged goods. A slut. A failure. A disappointment to my picture-perfect family as long as I can remember. I called off my wedding to William Bailey, the only man who thought I was worth fixing. A year later, he's marrying my sister. Unless I ask him not to . . .\"If you shatter, I'll find you . . . \"But now there's Asher Logan, a broken man who sees the fractures in my façade and doesn't want to fix me at all. Asher wants me to stop hiding, to stop pretending. Asher wants to break down my walls. But that means letting him see my ugly secrets and forgiving him for his. </p> <p>With my past weighing down on me, do I want the man who holds me together or the man who gives me permission to break? </p>"; 
